// TEST: Loop Array Return
// A plain (non-Poly) function RETURNING a loop-materialized array. The body's
// `a - scalar` broadcast is hoisted into a stage-2b materialization, and that
// materialized wrapper is the return value.
//
// This is the return-extent ABI. `Array<T,R>` stores a POINTER to its extents
// table, so a frame-local `size_t[R]` table made the wrapper unreturnable: the
// heap data pool survived the frame but the shape pointer dangled, and the
// caller's `c.extents[0]` read garbage past the real elements. The
// materialization now allocates the extents table on the heap — the same
// convention genApplyCombinator already used, which is why ITS array returns
// always worked — so the wrapper is self-describing across the call boundary
// and no caller-side extents plumbing is needed. Previously pinned as a
// codegen-stage reject-probe.
function center(a: T^1) -> T^1 = a - (reduce(a, (+)) / extents(a))
let x = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
let c = center(x)
// EXPECT: c = [-1, 0, 1]
